     "text": "<strong>description:</strong> three equal horizontal bands of cobalt blue (top), white, and cobalt blue, with the national coat of arms centered in the white band; the coat of arms has a round emblem with the words REPUBLICA DE EL SALVADOR EN LA AMERICA CENTRAL around it<br /><br /><strong>meaning:</strong> the blue bands stand for the Pacific Ocean and the Caribbean Sea, and the white for the land, as well as peace and prosperity<br /><br /><strong>history:</strong> the banner is based on the former blue-white-blue flag of the Federal Republic of Central America",
